{"step_index":295,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-27T02:46:59Z","thinking":"The user's question focuses on retrieving the bar time for the zigzag line. A prior statement might have implied `barIdx` holds this time data, prompting the clarification request. Need to verify that `barIdx` indeed stores the required time information or if there's a separate mechanism to access the candle/bar timestamp.\n\n\n`barIdx` is the index of a bar on the chart, a sequential number, not the actual time. The bar time, or `datetime`, represents the real time of the bar. It's crucial to obtain this bar time for reliability because `barIdx` resets on restart or new days. Data sources within the trading system provide this `datetime` information, not solely relying on the index.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"[Console]::OutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8\nSelect-String -Path \"Y:\\true_fractal\\fractal_zigzag.lua\", \"Y:\\split_fractal\\*.lua\" -Pattern \"time|barIdx|bar_idx|datetime\"","Cwd":"Y:\\true_fractal","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Checking time and barIdx in fractal scripts","toolSummary":"Search for time and barIdx in true_fractal and split_fractal"}}]}
